  "name": "CanthroFur",
  "shortName": null,
  "description": "CanthroFur is a furry convention and ski event held each January at a holiday village in Saint-Sauves-d'Auvergne, in central France, organized by SancyFur, a non-profit association. It grew out of informal furmeets at the home of the organizer Minevek, which centered on mountain walks, shared meals and conversation, and became a structured event with a group trip to a ski resort. The name combines \"Centre\" for its location in France, \"Anthro\" and \"Fur\". The convention has a strong identity built around local food and regional gastronomy, with local producers selling cheese, terrines, pâté and honey on site. From the second edition a shuttle bus has carried participants to and from the ski resort.",
